[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2992686153","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107769#issuecomment-2992686153","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107769","id":2992686153,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yYMRJ","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T20:16:57Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T20:16:57Z","body":"Should be fine for runtime shader generation on Intel Macs, but should be noted that when baking on Linux or Windows, `MOLTENVK_USED` won't be defined, so it will generate shaders that may not work on Intel macs using MoltenVK. \r\n\r\nIs it specific GPUs on Intel Macs that don't work? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2992686153/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2992698874","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107769#issuecomment-2992698874","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107769","id":2992698874,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yYPX6","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T20:25:09Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T20:25:09Z","body":"> but should be noted that when baking on Linux or Windows, MOLTENVK_USED won't be defined\r\n\r\nSame with `NO_IMAGE_ATOMICS` which is defined only on macOS and iOS and used in many places, so baking shaders for macOS/iOS from a non-mac system is likely already broken (for both Metal and Vulkan).\r\n\r\n> Is it specific GPUs on Intel Macs that don't work?\r\n\r\nNo idea, but the issue was recently encountered on AMD GPU and previously on Intel GPUs, so I assume it's a generic issue with all Intel macs.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2992698874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2992707125","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107769#issuecomment-2992707125","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107769","id":2992707125,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yYRY1","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T20:30:22Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T20:51:04Z","body":"> Same with `NO_IMAGE_ATOMICS` which is defined only on macOS and iOS and used in many places, so baking shaders for macOS/iOS from a non-mac system is likely already broken (for both Metal and Vulkan).\r\n\r\nGood point – I need to test `NO_IMAGE_ATOMICS` again. Some of that was to do with SPIRV-Cross issues, which I haven't revisited.\r\n\r\nI noticed @akien-mga is upgrading Vulkan SDKs in #107773. ~~I could do SPIRV-Cross separately and fix the Metal compilation (not hard).~~  @akien-mga has resolved it!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2992707125/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2992710932","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107769#issuecomment-2992710932","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107769","id":2992710932,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yYSUU","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T20:32:35Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T20:32:35Z","body":"In order to address that, additional context needs to be passed through the renderer, so that it can bake for different targets / platforms with different feature sets. I already started that in the Metal shader baker code, where I can pass OS + GPU to govern how the shaders are generated and compiled.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2992710932/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993045003","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107769#issuecomment-2993045003","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107769","id":2993045003,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yZj4L","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-20T22:27:08Z","updated_at":"2025-06-20T22:27:08Z","body":"> In order to address that, additional context needs to be passed through the renderer, so that it can bake for different targets / platforms with different feature sets. I already started that in the Metal shader baker code, where I can pass OS + GPU to govern how the shaders are generated and compiled.\r\n\r\nIn case on Metal it seems to be doing it on already compiled SPIRV code, this probably won't work with `define` (or will be overcomplicated). So it probably should do it by enabling/disabling shader variants on a source level, and `ShaderBakerExportPlugin` already do have information about target platform, I guess it only need a way to selectively pick variants depending on platform.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993045003/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3061816810","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107769#issuecomment-3061816810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107769","id":3061816810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62f53q","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T11:03:34Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T11:03:34Z","body":"Superseded by #107794","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3061816810/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]